  "VSCO 2 CE names the flute an octave low (its C3 sounds C4: the strongest partial and the fundamental sit at 261.6 Hz, nothing at 130.8 Hz). Every zone here is placed at the pitch it sounds, C4 to C7.",
  "The recordings are a spaced stereo pair whose channels partly cancel when summed (the steady part loses up to 8 dB in an L+R fold-down), so each file is mono from its louder channel (monoFrom on each layer). The two layers of a zone can come from different channels, which may sound slightly different in room tone.",
  "vib: layers of the same note disagree in pitch by more than 3 cents in 1 zones: E6 (v1-rr1 -1.2, v1-rr2 +3.0)",
  "nv: brightness does not rise with layer in 2 of 10 zones: C6 (v1 0.019, v2 0.010); E6 (v1 0.196, v2 0.006) (E6 v1 is a quiet take whose first 300 ms carry more breath than tone, which inflates the number)",
  "nv: C7 has one layer only (the library has no second one there); C6 and E6 use the library's v2 as the loud layer, the others its v3.",
  "vib has one dynamic layer (the library's v1) with two round-robin takes at C5, E5 and E6 (files -rr1 and -rr2).",
  "Levels are as recorded (not normalized); quiet layers sit low (nv C4 v1 peaks at -41 dBFS). Level by loopRmsDb.",
  "Four vib files (C4, A4, E5 rr1, C6) start with no silence: their very first sample is already only 54 to 58 dB below the peak, so they got a 2 ms fade-in (fadeInMs) against a start click; nothing else was changed at the start."
